    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **Josh Naylor**, who draws the highest efficiency score of 78.45. Facing a favorable matchup against Hughes (4.55 xERA) in a hitter-friendly park, **Naylor** benefits from a strong base projection and a +14% park adjustment, making him our safest bet for RBI production. Complementing him is **Brice Turang** (73.39), who remains a priority despite a tough matchup against Povich. While Povich is a lefty, the combination of a massive +16% park boost and the likelihood of **Turang** exploiting his elite speed against an opponent that allows a 57% stolen base success rate makes him a high-upside play for our scarcity-driven roster. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (69.59) provides an excellent floor; even batting at the bottom of the order, his efficiency is buoyed by a +13% platoon edge and the fact that opposing pitcher E. Rodriguez is highly susceptible to base runners.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult decision today involved the benching of **Austin Riley** (54.94). While **Riley**\u2019s base projections were solid, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Mickey Moniak** (64.11) and **Corbin Carroll** (63.74). **Moniak** is a particularly interesting start today; he draws a +14% platoon edge against Woo, which pushed his score well into the recommended starting tier. We are keeping a close eye on **Corbin Carroll**, whose +4% boost due to a slow delivery from Gerrit Cole suggests he could be a sneaky source of stolen bases despite the challenge of facing a premier arm.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding our lineup stability, as both **Moises Ballesteros** and **Jose Caballero** are still listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" While **Ballesteros** faces a difficult matchup against Prielipp, we are banking on his order placement to hold firm. Conversely, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** are set for challenging afternoons against elite-tier pitching in Gerrit Cole and Skenes, respectively. While these two have lower scores due to the quality of the opposing arms, their roles in the #3 hole provide enough volume to justify their inclusion in today\u2019s rotation.",
